// @emit-error only i32[] arrays and struct/union element arrays are supported
// @hint redundant type annotation: `a` is inferred as `{v: i32}[]`
// FALSE-REJECT xfail. This program is SOUND and SHOULD compile; it errors. NOT an
// unsoundness — the compiler refuses a valid program. The `xfail-false-reject-`
// prefix is the corpus's rejects-too-much kind; see README.vl. The `@error` pins the
// UNDESIRED diagnostic so the gap's closure is loud rather than silent.
//
// THE GAP: an INLINE union whose arms are arrays of STRUCTURALLY IDENTICAL structs.
// A union's members are deduped structurally, so `A[] | B[]` — where `A` and `B` are
// both `{v:i32}` — collapses to a single member and takes that member's type. The
// annotation node then records a plain `TyArray`, not a `TyUnion`.
//
// `emit_collect`'s array rung skips array VALIDATION for a union whose last arm is an
// array (its ref-array arms are interned by `markRefArrayArms` on the union path).
// That skip asks "is this node's type a union?" — and for the collapsed shape the
// honest answer is no, so the union spelling `A[]|B[]` falls into `checkArrName` and
// is rejected as a non-i32 array.
//
// Three neighbours all compile clean, which is what makes this the narrow case:
//   - DIFFERENT shapes, inline:  `A[] | C[]`   (members survive dedup -> a real union)
//   - SAME shapes, DECLARED:     `type Both = A[] | B[]`  (matched by name/index)
//   - SAME shapes, non-array:    `Cat | Dog`   (B107 — declines to the name, correctly)
//
// PRE-EXISTING: reproduced on the compiler at 08647012^, i.e. before the arena union
// rung (#1592) existed, so it is not a regression from that conversion. It is the
// same root cause B107 measured at the variant param rung — structural dedup erasing
// a distinction the spelling still carries — surfacing here as a reject instead of a
// wrong answer.
//
// EXPECTED: compiles clean and prints 1. ACTUAL: the emit error pinned above.
//
// TODO(destringify): the union question needs an arm-count that survives dedup, or
// the array rung needs to consult the ANNOTATION's arm structure rather than the
// collapsed type. See docs/internals/destringify-types-program.md B108.
type A = { v: i32 }
type B = { v: i32 }

function pick(xs: A[] | B[]) {
  if xs is A[] { return 1 }
  return 2
}

const a: A[] = [{ v: 1 }]
print(pick(a))
